{"text":"மகளிர்","lemma":"makaḷir","gloss":"women"},{"text":"க்கு","lemma":"kku","gloss":"dative suffix"}],"gloss":"to the women"},{"surface":"உறுதிணை","parts":[{"text":"உறு","lemma":"uṟu","gloss":"firm/great"},{"text":"திணை","lemma":"tiṇai","gloss":"support/refuge"}],"gloss":"firm support"},{"surface":"ஆகி","parts":[{"text":"ஆகு","lemma":"āku","gloss":"to become"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"having been"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தன்","parts":[{"text":"தன்","lemma":"தன்","gloss":"his"}],"gloss":"his","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"துணை","parts":[{"text":"துணை","lemma":"tuṇai","gloss":"companion"}],"gloss":"companion"},{"surface":"ஆயம்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயம்","lemma":"āyam","gloss":"group of friends"}],"gloss":"group of friends"},{"surface":"மறந்தனன்","parts":[{"text":"மறந்தனன்","lemma":"மறந்தனன்","gloss":"he forgot"}],"gloss":"he forgot","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கொல்லோ","parts":[{"text":"கொல்","lemma":"kol","gloss":"clitic of doubt"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ō","gloss":"clitic of lament"}],"gloss":"alas"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பகைவர்ப்","parts":[{"text":"பகைவர்ப்","lemma":"பகைவர்ப்","gloss":"enemies"}],"gloss":"enemies","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பிணிக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"பிணி","lemma":"piṇi","gloss":"to bind"},{"text":"க்","lemma":"k","gloss":"future marker"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"binding"},{"surface":"ஆற்றல்","parts":[{"text":"ஆற்றல்","lemma":"āṟṟal","gloss":"strength/power"}],"gloss":"strength"},{"surface":"நசைவர்க்கு","parts":[{"text":"நசைவர்","lemma":"nacaivar","gloss":"those who desire/bards"},{"text":"க்கு","lemma":"kku","gloss":"dative suffix"}],"gloss":"to those who desire"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அளந்து","parts":[{"text":"அள","lemma":"aḷa","gloss":"to measure"},{"text":"ந்து","lemma":"ntu","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"measuring"},{"surface":"கொடை","parts":[{"text":"கொடை","lemma":"koṭai","gloss":"gift/generosity"}],"gloss":"generosity"},{"surface":"அறியா","parts":[{"text":"அறி","lemma":"aṟi","gloss":"to know"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ā","gloss":"negative suffix"}],"gloss":"not knowing"},{"surface":"ஈகை","parts":[{"text":"ஈகை","lemma":"īkai","gloss":"giving/charity"}],"gloss":"giving"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மணிவரை","parts":[{"text":"மணி","lemma":"maṇi","gloss":"sapphire/gem"},{"text":"வரை","lemma":"varai","gloss":"mountain"}],"gloss":"sapphire mountain"},{"surface":"அன்ன","parts":[{"text":"அன்ன","lemma":"anna","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"},{"surface":"மாஅயோனே","parts":[{"text":"மா","lemma":"mā","gloss":"dark/great"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"alapetai filler"},{"text":"ஓன்","lemma":"ōṉ","gloss":"he who is"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"clitic"}],"gloss":"he of dark hue"}]}],"literal":"In the swaying, fiery Krittika constellation / in the dense darkness of midnight / with the bent palmyra star as the root / so that the water in the pond-like constellation dries up / in the high expanse of the month of Panguni / as the first star Uttiram deviated from its position / and the fixed star Mrigasira rose opposite to it / and the ancient star Krittika set in the western horizon / without going north, without approaching south / as a lamp to the ocean-girdled earth / spreading intense fire, rising against the wind and raging / a meteor fell from the sky. / Seeing that, we and other various bards / of the lord of the good country with drum-sounding waterfalls / prayed, \"If he is free from illness, it is indeed good!\" / with broken hearts and perishing minds spreading grief. / We feared, and the seventh day has come today! / Strong elephants sleep placing their trunks down, / strongly bound drums roll with torn heads, / the guarding white umbrella lies with its staff broken and withered, / and spirited horses languish without their swift gait, / because he has reached the world of the heavenly beings. / Being the firm support to women with bright bangles, / did he forget his own companion group, alas? / He who has the power to bind enemies, / who knows no measure in giving to those who desire, / like a sapphire mountain, he of dark hue!","translation":"In the dense darkness of midnight, amidst the swaying fiery Krittika constellation, with the bent palmyra star at its root, as the waters of the pond-like constellation heated up, in the high sky of the month of Panguni, the leading star Uttiram shifted its place. The fixed star Mrigasira rose opposite to it, while the ancient Krittika set in the west. Without drifting north or south, like a lamp to the ocean-girdled earth, a meteor fell from the sky, raging against the wind and spreading intense fire. Seeing this, we and other bards of the good country of drum-sounding waterfalls prayed with trembling hearts, 'May our king be free from illness!' We feared, and today the seventh day has arrived. The mighty elephants sleep with their trunks cast down; the tightly bound drums roll with torn heads; the protective white umbrella lies withered with its staff broken; and the swift, spirited horses stand listless. He has departed to the world of the gods. Having been the sole refuge of women wearing bright bangles, has he forgotten his beloved companions? He who bound his enemies with power, whose boundless generosity knew no measure, the dark-hued king who stood like a sapphire mountain!","modern":"அசைகின்ற கார்த்திகை மீன் கூட்டத்துடனும், நிறைந்த இருளையுடைய நள்ளிரவிலும், வளைந்த பனை போன்ற அனுராத மீனை வேராகக் கொண்டு, குளத்தின் கடைப் பகுதியில் நீர் காயுமாறு, பங்குனி மாதத்து உயர்ந்த ஆகாயத்தில், முதன்மை நாளாகிய உத்திர மீன் தன் நிலையிலிருந்து மாற, அதற்கு எதிரே மிருகசீரிட மீன் எழ, பழைய கார்த்திகை மீன் மேற்றிசையில் மறைய, வடதிசை நோக்கிச் செல்லாமலும் தென்திசை நெருங்காமலும், கடலிடத்து விளக்குப் போலப் பெருநெருப்பைப் பரப்பிக் காற்றுடன் பொங்கி ஒரு மீன் வானிலிருந்து விழுந்தது. அதனைக் கண்டு நாங்களும் பிற இரவலர்களும், அருவிகள் பாயும் நல்நாட்டின் தலைவன் நோயின்றி வாழ வேண்டும் என்று அஞ்சினோம். ஆனால் ஏழாம் நாள் அவன் இறந்துவிட்டான். யானைகள் துயில்கின்றன; முரசுகள் கிழிந்து கிடக்கின்றன; வெண்கொற்றக்குடை சாய்ந்து கிடக்கிறது; குதிரைகள் இயக்கம் இன்றி நிற்கின்றன. அவன் மேலுலகம் எய்தினான். வளையல் அணிந்த மகளிர்க்குத் துணையாக இருந்த அவன் தன் சுற்றத்தாரை மறந்துவிட்டானோ? பகைவரை வெல்லும் ஆற்றலும், இரவலர்க்குக் கணக்கின்றி வழங்கும் கொடையும் கொண்ட, மணிமலை போன்ற கரிய நிறமுடைய அவன் இறந்துவிட்டான்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Puram genre and is a moving lament (kaiyaṟunilai) sung by the poet Kūdalūr Kiḻār on the death of the Chera king Yāṉaikkaṭcēy Māntarañcēral Irumpoṟai. The poet describes a terrifying astronomical event—a massive meteor falling from the sky in the month of Panguni—which was seen as a dire omen. Fearing for the king's life, the poet and other bards prayed for his safety, but their worst fears came true exactly seven days later. The poem vividly depicts the grief-stricken kingdom where royal elephants sleep in sorrow, drums lie broken, and the white umbrella of state is cast down. The king is praised for his boundless generosity and compared to a majestic sapphire mountain.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}